# Line endings, settled once.
#
# git is configured with core.autocrlf=true on at least one machine here, which stores LF and
# checks out CRLF on Windows. `deno fmt` wants LF and reports every file as unformatted when it
# meets CRLF, so `deno task verify` fails locally on Windows and passes in CI on Linux, which is
# the worst way for a check to be wrong: it looks like the Windows machine is broken.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform makes the formatter, the repository and CI
# agree. Editors have handled LF on Windows for a decade.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches their bytes looking for line endings.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
